1g. unarc-rs ARJ reader — MIT OR Apache-2.0 (source derivative)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The ARJ reader in crates/exav-unpack/src/formats/arj_parse/ is vendored and
adapted from the `unarc-rs` crate — multi-volume support, volume providers, and
external error types removed; wired to `delharc` for LH6 decompression.
Dual-licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0; the MIT or Apache terms apply at the
distributor's choice (both reproduced/referenced elsewhere in this file).

The ZOO structures in crates/exav-unpack/src/formats/zoo_parse.rs are vendored
and adapted from the same crate, for the same reason the ARJ reader was: linking
it brings in a second `zip` with default features, and Cargo's feature
unification then enables the `zip` crate's own LZMA/bzip2/deflate64 decoders
inside exav, bypassing exav's per-member budget. Adapted to exav's error
handling, with the variable-length part of a directory entry (long filename,
directory name) actually read.

The ZOO test archives in crates/exav-unpack/tests/fixtures/zoo/ (`store.zoo`,
`default.zoo`, `high_per.zoo`) are that project's own test corpus, redistributed
under the same terms. They hold one identical member under the three
compression methods, which is what lets the codecs be checked against stored
bytes rather than against themselves.

Upstream: https://github.com/mkrueger/unarc-rs
Copyright (c) Mike Krüger.


