1h1. iced-x86 — MIT (generated opcode tables)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

crates/exav-x86/src/generated.rs holds the SIMD, system and VEX regions of the
x86 opcode maps. It is not hand-written and not transcribed from a manual: it is
emitted by crates/exav-x86/tools/gen-tables, which decodes a probe for every
(prefix, opcode, /digit, mod) combination with `iced-x86` and records what came
back. The tables are therefore derived from `iced-x86`'s data, and the MIT
License requires retaining its copyright and permission notice (the MIT text is
in the exav LICENSE file).

`iced-x86` is also the oracle that exav-x86's differential tests and the
`x86_decode` fuzz target compare against — including the decoding that
exav-pe-emu drives. It is a dev-dependency only: the decoder exav-pe-emu uses at
run time is exav-x86, and no iced code reaches a shipped artifact.

Upstream: https://github.com/icedland/iced
Copyright (C) 2018-present iced project and contributors.


